## Completed Work (across sessions)

1. Clipboard paste fix: `use_clipboard=1` now correctly pastes from system clipboard
2. Default `use_clipboard` changed to 1
3. Undo support for `:%s/pat/rep/g`
4. `:%s/pat/rep` (without g flag) — replace first occurrence per line
5. Status line timeout behavior fix
6. Comprehensive visual mode tests (42 tests, all passing)
7. Visual mode bug fixes (gv reselect, line navigation, case ops)
8. Search forward/backward fix (unpack tuple correctly)
9. Word search * / # fix (non-US keyboard AltGr detection)
10. Debug key logging (`--debug-key` option)
11. Project handoff file (`.handoff`) added to repo for cross-session continuity
12. Keyboard dispatch architecture documentation (`doc/keyboard-dispatch.md`)
13. Fix vim_completion.t: add missing `use lib ('lib', 't/lib')` so Perl can locate Completion.pm
14. Fix vim_replace.t: add cursor advance in VimBuffer::Test::replace_char() (was using substr without moving cursor)
15. Fix vim_plugin.t: wire PluginLoader into create_test_context() so plugins are loaded, keymaps merged, and ex-commands registered
16. Fix t/00-smoke-mock.t: replace 4 hardcoded paths with FindBin::($RealBin) for portability
17. Fix stale visual highlight after undo/redo: clear selection (first approach)
18. Undo/redo highlight: GtkTextTag with paragraph-background for subtle tint of restored content
    - CSS approach failed (GtkSourceView ignores CSS selection override)
    - `background` tag property only covers text, `paragraph-background` fills full widget width
    - GTK selection collapsed after tag applied so native color doesn't paint over tint
    - Delta ~5% (12/255) for subtle effect; lighter in dark theme, darker in light theme
    - Tag auto-removed on next keypress via _clear_undo_highlight in handle_normal_mode
19. Font zoom: `+`/`-` keys in normal mode to increase/decrease font size
    - `_recalc_page_size` extracted as shared helper (was duplicated in two places)
    - `_zoom_font` changes font via Pango::FontDescription, min 6pt
    - page_size and line_height recalculated after every font change
    - Count prefix supported (e.g., `3+` increases by 3 points)
    - Numpad keys (KP_Add, KP_Subtract) also wired
20. `gi` command: resume insert mode at last exit position
    - `last_insert_pos` saved in $ctx when exiting insert mode (Insert.pm)
    - `insert_at_last` action restores position and enters insert mode (Normal.pm)
    - Clamped to buffer bounds if buffer changed since last insert
    - Falls back to `i` behavior if no prior insert position recorded
    - 4 tests in vim_editing.t (422 total tests, all passing)
21. Consolidated documentation: moved `docs/keyboard-dispatch.md` to `doc/`

## Key Architectural Notes

- **Dispatch flow**: Key event → `_dispatch` in VimBindings.pm → routes to mode handler
- **Modes**: normal, insert, visual, visual_line, visual_block, command_line
- **Test infrastructure**: `t/lib/` has mock GTK objects; `Gtk3::SourceEditor::VimBuffer::Test` is the mock buffer
- **Documentation**: `doc/keyboard-dispatch.md` covers the full dispatch architecture for all modes
- **prove** does NOT work from this directory; must cd into /home/z/my-project/P5-Gtk3-SourceEditor first
- Push workflow: commit in submodule → cd to z repo → git add submodule → commit → push

## Important Process Rules (from user — NEVER violate these)

1. **Read files SEQUENTIALLY** — never read in parallel, it breaks frequently
2. **Keep this handoff file updated** — update it whenever state changes, always update before pushing
3. **Commit messages must be descriptive** — explain what was done, not just "update"
4. **Make small commits** — one commit per logical unit of work / functionality completed
5. **Show commit messages in chat** — after committing, print the commit(s) so the user sees them
6. **Always update the handoff before pushing to remote** — the handoff should reflect the state being pushed
7. **The handoff file is tracked in the repo** — add it to the submodule and commit it
8. **Do NOT re-do work already completed** — read this file first, check git log, check test results before starting anything
9. **If you don't know what state something is in, check git log and run tests before guessing**
